A||||4||G25C||A/C or Defrost make the engine chug
Z||000000||G25C||08-26-99||11:45 PM||||<br>If i turn on the A/C or the defrost, Instently i feel a great deal of engine loss pulling on the motor.  And then it will do this about every minute or so.  Slight "pulling chugs" like if you were to veryly lightly push on the brake and let off real quick.  <p>And if i leave the A/C or defrost on when im in gear (87 GT) and not going anywhere, just idling.  I hear a loud squealing/welping noise (kinda like a wet fan belt makes) and it doesnt go away untill i turn the a/c or defrost off.<p>anyone got a clue
Z||000001||JetroGT||08-26-99||11:57 PM||||A bad compressor/belt.
Z||000002||G25C||08-27-99||12:16 AM||||thanks Jetro, is this easy to change?  Im used to working on 20 year old (or older) firebirds.
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||08-27-99||12:58 AM||||G25C,<br>I had a problem like that on my car I looked at the belts and thought they were fine maybe  just wet?, well one day I took a good hard look and that was just it.....HARD belts. They were tight and looked fine but the heat over time will make them hard and dry. that was the pulling feel and squeal.<p>Fixed it with new ones. Give it a try it doesn`t take much time or money.
Z||000004||ChadMan||08-27-99||08:15 AM||||I bet your A/C compressor is getting ready to go.  Right before mine seized up, it felt like it was taking 25 or 30 hp to run the A/C.
